ZenX - Product Requirements Document (PRD)
Version: 1.0
Date: November 11, 2025
Project Type: Fitness Tracking Application
Status: Implementation Ready

1. Executive Summary
ZenX is a comprehensive fitness tracking application inspired by the Heavy fitness tracker. The application enables users to track workouts, exercises, sets, reps, and monitor their fitness progress over time. ZenX will be built using a modern, scalable microservices architecture with cross-platform support for Web, Android, iOS, and WatchOS.
1.1 Project Goals

Build a production-ready fitness tracking platform
Ensure cross-platform compatibility (Web, Mobile, Wearables)
Implement scalable microservices architecture
Provide real-time workout tracking capabilities
Enable comprehensive progress analytics and insights


2. Technology Stack
2.1 Frontend

Framework: Flutter
Platforms: Web, Android, iOS, WatchOS
API Communication: GraphQL Client
Rationale: Single codebase for all platforms, native performance, rich UI components

2.2 Backend Services

Language: Go (Golang)
Architecture: Microservices
API Gateway: GraphQL Federation
Inter-Service Communication: gRPC with Protocol Buffers
Rationale: High performance, strong typing, excellent concurrency support

2.3 Data Layer

Primary Database: PostgreSQL
Rationale:

Relational data model (Users → Workouts → Exercises → Sets)
ACID compliance for data integrity
Excellent support for complex queries and analytics
Native JSON support for flexible schema extensions
Strong time-series data capabilities



2.4 Infrastructure & DevOps

Containerization: Docker
Orchestration: Kubernetes
Infrastructure as Code: Terraform
Message Queue/Event Streaming: NATS
Service Mesh: Istio (implied with Kubernetes)
Monitoring & Observability: Prometheus, Grafana, Jaeger (distributed tracing)

2.5 Environments

Development (dev): For active development and testing
Production (prod): Live environment serving end users


